<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">José Gregorio Monagas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1795">1795</a>–<a href="/years/1858">1858</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">José Gregorio Monagas was a Venezuelan general of the War of Independence and president from 1851 to 1855, succeeding his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-tadeo-monagas">José Tadeo Monagas</a> during the decade of Liberal rule known as the Monagas era. His government decreed the abolition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> on 24 March 1854. Imprisoned after the fall of his brother's regime in 1858, he died in custody in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maracaibo">Maracaibo</a> that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jose-gregorio-monagas.jpg" alt="José Gregorio Monagas" width="320" height="358" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jos%C3%A9_Gregorio_Monagas_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
